# memflow-muse Portfolio Rules

## Identity

This is Amit Chakraborty's personal portfolio, built as a live mem0 API demo
for a Staff/Principal Frontend Engineer application at mem0.ai.

**Stack:** TanStack Start + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui + Bun

---

## Design System — Never Break These

- **Light theme only.** No dark mode. No `prefers-color-scheme`. No dark backgrounds
  except terminal panels (`#1A1D23`) in the Logs and Demo sections.
- **One accent color:** `--signal: #16A07C` (mem0 emerald). Never add a second accent.
- **Fonts:** Instrument Serif (display), Geist (body), JetBrains Mono (code/labels).
  Never use Inter, Roboto, or Arial as display fonts.
- **All colors** via CSS custom properties from `src/styles.css`. No hardcoded hex
  values outside the PROJECTS data array and cluster color definitions.
- **Spacing:** 8px base grid. Use multiples of 4px.
- **Animations:** CSS keyframes or inline style transitions only.
  No Framer Motion — this project deliberately avoids it.

---

## Code Style

- **TypeScript strict** — no `any`, no non-null assertions without comments.
- **Functional components only.** No class components.
- **Inline styles** for all portfolio component layout/positioning.
  Tailwind classes only for shadcn/ui primitives.
- **No console.log** in committed code.
- **All interactive elements** need `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`.
- **Focus rings** must be visible: `outline: 2px solid var(--signal)`.

---

## File Architecture

- `src/components/portfolio/portfolio.tsx` — All portfolio sections live here.
  This is intentional: one file, one scroll, one artifact. Don't split it up.
- `src/lib/api/memory.functions.ts` — Server functions only. No UI imports.
- `src/lib/mem0/mock-client.ts` — Client-side mock only. No server-only imports.

---

## mem0 API Rules

- Server functions in `memory.functions.ts` always return:
  `{ success: boolean; data: T; error?: string; apiMode: "real" | "mock" }`
- The Demo component catches server function errors and falls back to the mock
  client silently — the demo must NEVER break.
- `apiMode: "real"` shows a green "● API Connected" indicator.
  `apiMode: "mock"` shows amber "○ Local Demo Mode".

---

## What NOT to Change

- The `Section` component's fade-up animation — one-shot via IntersectionObserver.
- The `HeroStagger` component — stagger timing is calibrated.
- `public/sw.js` cache version — bump it manually after significant asset changes.
- The `PROJECTS` array `id` values — they're displayed as mem0 memory IDs.

---

## When Adding a Project

Always include all 8 fields in the Project interface:
`id, name, signal, tagline, category, score, year, url, impact, stack, description,
roleHighlights (3 items), whyItMatters`.

The `whyItMatters` field is the mem0-specific insight shown in the project modal.
It must connect the project to mem0's memory architecture in a concrete, specific way.

---

## Commit Messages

Use conventional commits:
- `feat:` new section or feature
- `fix:` bug fix
- `style:` design/CSS changes
- `perf:` performance improvement
- `docs:` CLAUDE.md, PROMPTS.md, README changes
- `chore:` dependencies, config
